.\" Manual page for scribobulate's configuration files, section 5.
.\"
.\" THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE, not a generated artefact. Packaging substitutes
.\" @VERSION@ and @DATE@ and installs the result.
.\"
.\" IT IS A THIRD COPY OF A VOCABULARY, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS GATED. The theme
.\" keys are declared once in src/theme/keys.rs (the `keys!` table), described
.\" for developers in sdd/SCHEMA.md, and described for users here; the
.\" config.toml settings are declared in src/config.rs and described here.
.\" `cargo xtask lint-references` check 16 fails when any of those vocabularies
.\" disagrees, in either direction. What it CANNOT check is whether a
.\" description is still TRUE -- a key renamed nowhere but retyped, or given a
.\" new default, passes. Re-read the prose when you change a key's meaning;
.\" the gate only guarantees no key is silently added or dropped (ScrAP-123 is
.\" the species it does close: a fact restated in prose with nothing comparing
.\" it to its source).
.TH SCRIBOBULATE 5 "@DATE@" "scribobulate @VERSION@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
scribobulate \- configuration and reading-theme files for scribobulate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/scribobulate/config.toml
.br
.I ~/.config/scribobulate/themes.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR scribobulate (1)
reads two optional TOML files. Neither has to exist.
.PP
.I config.toml
holds application settings \(em window size, page margins, the code font. It is
read once at startup from the user configuration directory only; there is no
system-wide copy.
.PP
.I themes.toml
holds the preview reading themes: the colours, typography and decoration
geometry the rendered document is drawn with. It is searched for in several
places and merged, so a user file can adjust a single key of a shipped theme
without restating it.
.PP
.B A malformed file never prevents startup.
A file that does not parse is reported in the log and ignored. Within a file
that does parse, an unrecognised key is reported and skipped, and an
out-of-range value is clamped to its stated range rather than rejected. The
worst outcome of a bad theme is a decoration that is absent.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
.I config.toml
has four sections, all optional, and every key within them is optional. An
omitted key takes the default shown.
.SS [window]
.TP
.BR width " (integer, default " 900 )
Width in pixels of a new window, when no session is restored.
.TP
.BR height " (integer, default " 720 )
Height in pixels of a new window, when no session is restored.
.SS [view]
Page margins for the preview, in pixels.
.TP
.BR left_margin " (integer, default " 20 )
Space between the window edge and the text column, left.
.TP
.BR right_margin " (integer, default " 20 )
Space between the window edge and the text column, right.
.TP
.BR top_margin " (integer, default " 16 )
Space above the first block of the document.
.TP
.BR bottom_margin " (integer, default " 16 )
Space below the last block of the document.
.SS [code]
.TP
.BR font " (string, default " monospace )
CSS font-family string for inline code and fenced code blocks.
.TP
.BR block_padding " (integer, default " 12 )
Padding inside a fenced code block, in pixels.
.TP
.BR light_theme " (string, default " InspiredGitHub )
Syntax-highlighting theme used when the desktop is light. Also settable per
reading theme; see
.B syntect_theme
below, which takes precedence.
.TP
.BR dark_theme " (string, default " base16-ocean.dark )
Syntax-highlighting theme used when the desktop is dark.
.SS [outline]
.TP
.BR width " (integer, default " 240 )
Default width in pixels of the document-outline sidebar.
.SS Example
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[window]
width = 1200
height = 900

[view]
left_margin = 48
right_margin = 48

[code]
font = "JetBrains Mono, monospace"
light_theme = "Solarized (light)"
.fi
.RE
.SH READING THEMES
.SS Search path
The first file found at each row is read; all of them are merged, per theme id
and per key, with earlier rows winning.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
1.  ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/scribobulate/themes.toml
2.  ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/scribobulate/themes.toml
3.  each $XDG_DATA_DIRS entry -> .../scribobulate/themes.toml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Because the merge is per key, a user file may override one key of a shipped
theme, override an application-wide default through the
.B [themes.system]
block, or define an entirely new theme. A theme the application does not ship
appears in the theme chooser alongside the built-in ones.
.SS File structure
Each theme is a table named for its id:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[themes.midnight]
name = "Midnight"
symbol = "\(bu"
background = "#11131a"
foreground = "#d6d9e0"
heading_color_h1 = "#8fb7ff"
heading_band_color_h1 = "#1b2030"
link_underline = "none"
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B [themes.system]
is an ordinary theme with one extra role: it is where a value the application
would otherwise derive for itself is stated. No key is system-only and no theme
is second-class.
.SS Key resolution
Each key resolves at the first source that states it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
1.  the selected theme's specific key   (heading_color_h2, list_marker_color_3)
2.  the selected theme's bare key       (heading_color, list_marker_color)
3.  [themes.system]'s specific key
4.  [themes.system]'s bare key
5.  the key's own default, or a value derived from the desktop theme
.fi
.RE
.PP
A theme's own bare key therefore outranks
.BR [themes.system] 's
specific one. An unset key means
.IR "not present" ,
never
.IR guess :
a decoration nobody asks for is not drawn.
.SS Key naming
A key's suffix states its type.
.TP
.B _color
A colour. So are the paired
.B _bg
and
.B _fg
spellings, which are a surface's fill and its ink; the page's own pair is
spelled
.B background
and
.BR foreground .
.TP
.B _sprite
A path to an image, drawn or tiled in place of a flat value. Relative to the
directory of the
.I themes.toml
that states it. Absolute paths, and any path leaving that directory, are
refused; so is an extension other than
.IR png ", " webp " or " jpg ,
an oversized file, and an image whose pixel dimensions are implausibly large. A
refused sprite is logged and the decoration is simply absent.
.TP
.B _glyph
A short string drawn in place of a marker the application would otherwise draw.
Refused if empty, longer than 8 characters, or carrying a control character.
.TP
.BR _h1 " \(em " _h5
Narrows a heading key to one level.
.TP
.BR _2 ", " _3
Narrows a list key to one nesting depth.
.PP
Colours are strings:
.IR #RRGGBB ", " #RRGGBBAA ", " #RRGGBB_AA ", or a CSS colour name."
The underscored form is a colour plus a hex alpha byte.
.PP
.B No key takes an array.
Anything that varies by heading level or list depth is stated as a suffixed key,
one value each.
.PP
.B A sprite outranks its flat sibling.
Where a decoration has both a
.B _sprite
and a colour or glyph, a theme that states both gets the sprite; the other value
is ignored rather than composited under it.
.PP
Pixel metrics are design-time values at a zoom of 1.0 and are scaled with the
view. Every metric is clamped to the range given with it.
.SS Heading levels
Every key in
.B Headings
below may be written bare, applying to every level, or suffixed
.BR _h1 " \(em " _h5
to apply to one. There are five levels, not six: a level-6 heading is drawn as a
level 5, so no key spells
.BR _h6 .
Where a default varies by level it is given below as five values in order.
.SH THEME KEYS
Every key is optional; omitting one means "derive or inherit it".
.SS Base
.TP
.B name
String. Display name in the theme chooser. Defaults to the theme id.
.TP
.B symbol
String. Decorative symbol shown left of the name in the chooser.
.TP
.B background
Colour. Page background. One of the three base colours every derived colour
follows from.
.TP
.B foreground
Colour. Body text.
.TP
.B accent_color
Colour. Accent colour.
.TP
.B font_family
String. Body font stack. Always terminated with a generic family.
.TP
.B syntect_theme
String. Syntax-highlighting theme for code blocks. Chosen by the
.IR page 's
luminance rather than the desktop's when unset.
.SS Headings
.TP
.B heading_color
Colour. Heading ink. Defaults to the body foreground. A link inside a heading
still takes the link colour.
.TP
.B heading_font
String. Heading font stack. Defaults to
.BR font_family .
.TP
.B heading_scale
Number. Size relative to the body. Default 2.2 \(bu 1.8 \(bu 1.48 \(bu 1.2 \(bu
1.0. Clamped 0.25\-8.0.
.TP
.B heading_weight
Integer, default 700. Clamped 100\-1000.
.TP
.B heading_overline
.IR none " or " single ", default " none .
A rule above the heading text, in the heading's own ink. There is deliberately
no overline colour key.
.TP
.B heading_underline
.IR none ", " single ", " double " or " wavy ", default " none .
A rule below the heading text \(em the decoration line under the glyphs, not a
column-width divider.
.TP
.B heading_underline_color
Colour. The below-rule's colour. Omitted, it follows the heading's ink.
.TP
.B heading_band_color
Colour. A band behind the heading's text, spanning the content column and
surviving soft-wrap as one continuous band. Absent means that level carries no
band.
.TP
.B heading_band_gradient_to_color
Colour. A second stop: the band becomes a vertical gradient down to this
colour. Ignored where the level states no fill.
.TP
.B heading_band_sprite
Sprite. Tiled at its natural size across the band in place of its fill.
Outranks the fill and the gradient.
.TP
.B heading_band_radius
Integer, default 0. Corner radius of the band. Clamped 0\-400. Not drawn in an
exported PDF.
.TP
.B heading_band_padding
Integer, default 12. Space between the band's edge and the text inside it, each
side. Clamped 0\-400. Applied only to a level that carries a band.
.TP
.B heading_space_above
Integer, default 0. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B heading_space_below
Integer. Default 4 \(bu 4 \(bu 2 \(bu 2 \(bu 2. Clamped 0\-400.
.SS Body and inline text
.TP
.B bold_weight
Integer, default 700. Clamped 100\-1000.
.TP
.B supsub_scale
Number, default 0.72. Superscript and subscript size. Clamped 0.25\-8.0.
.TP
.B superscript_rise
Integer, default 4. Clamped \-64\-64.
.TP
.B subscript_rise
Integer, default \-2. Clamped \-64\-64.
.TP
.B strikethrough_color
Colour. The line through
.IR ~~text~~ .
Omitted, it follows the struck text's own ink.
.TP
.B mark_bg
Colour, default
.IR #fff59d_88 .
Background band behind
.I ==marked==
text.
.TP
.B mark_fg
Colour. Ink for marked text. Omitted, marked text keeps the body foreground and
only its background changes \(em which is how a highlighter behaves on paper.
State it when the band is opaque enough to need its own ink.
.TP
.B code_inline_bg
Colour. Inline code-span background.
.TP
.B code_block_bg
Colour. Fenced code-block background.
.SS Links
.TP
.B link_color
Colour. Link ink.
.TP
.B link_underline
.IR none ", " single ", " double " or " wavy ", default " single .
.TP
.B link_underline_color
Colour. Stated independently of the link's ink; omitted, the line follows it.
.SS Lists
The three keys marked
.B (tiered)
also take
.B _2
and
.B _3
forms \(em the bullet at nesting depth 2, and at depth 3 and deeper. Each falls
back to the next shallower tier rather than to the bare key, so stating only the
.B _2
form reaches every depth from 2 down. Only bullets are tiered: a nested numeral
is still a numeral and a nested task box is still a box.
.TP
.B list_marker_color \fR(tiered)\fP
Colour. Bullet, numeral and task-checkbox ink; the item's text keeps the body
foreground. The bare key colours all three marker kinds, but its
.BR _2 / _3
forms are bullet only.
.TP
.B list_task_marker_color
Colour. The task checkbox, in both states. Defaults to
.BR list_marker_color .
.TP
.B list_bullet_glyph \fR(tiered)\fP
Glyph drawn in place of the bullet dot.
.TP
.B list_ordered_glyph
Glyph drawn in place of the ordered numeral. This discards the ordinal.
.TP
.B list_task_glyph
Glyph drawn in place of the unchecked task box.
.TP
.B list_task_checked_glyph
Glyph drawn in place of the checked task box. Resolves independently of the
unchecked one.
.TP
.B list_bullet_sprite \fR(tiered)\fP
Sprite drawn in place of the bullet dot.
.TP
.B list_ordered_sprite
Sprite drawn in place of the ordered numeral.
.TP
.B list_task_sprite
Sprite drawn in place of the unchecked task box.
.TP
.B list_task_checked_sprite
Sprite drawn in place of the checked task box.
.TP
.B list_step
Integer, default 28. Indent added per nesting depth. Clamped 4\-400.
.TP
.B list_item_gap
Integer, default 8. Space between items. Clamped 0\-400.
.SS Blockquote
.TP
.B blockquote_bar_color
Colour. The quote's accent bar.
.TP
.B blockquote_bar_sprite
Sprite tiled at its natural size down the accent bar. The tile is clipped to the
bar, so set
.B blockquote_bar_width
to the tile's own width.
.TP
.B blockquote_bar_width
Integer, default 3. Clamped 0\-400. With
.B blockquote_text_gap
it is also the per-level step by which a nested quote indents, to a cap of six
levels.
.TP
.B blockquote_text_gap
Integer, default 10. Bar to quoted text. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B blockquote_bg
Colour. A panel behind quoted text; absent unless stated. It does not nest \(em a
quote inside a quote inherits its parent's fill rather than painting a second
panel over it, so a translucent value is composited once however deep the
nesting goes.
.TP
.B blockquote_fg
Colour. The ink quoted body text takes. A link, heading or mark inside the quote
keeps its own colour.
.SS Table
.TP
.B table_border_color
Colour.
.TP
.B table_border_width
Integer, default 1. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B table_head_bg
Colour. Header-row background.
.TP
.B table_head_fg
Colour. Header-row ink. Omitted, it takes the bare
.BR heading_color ;
omitting that too leaves it on the body ink.
.TP
.B table_cell_padding_v
Integer, default 4. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B table_cell_padding_h
Integer, default 10. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B table_cell_radius
Integer, default 0. Corner radius of a table cell and of nothing else. Clamped
0\-400. Not drawn in an exported PDF.
.SS Disclosure
The
.RI < details >
indicator is a two-state control and takes one colour key for both states; the
glyph is what carries the state, and the two glyph and sprite keys resolve
independently.
.PP
The five indicator keys \(em
.BR disclosure_marker_color ,
the two glyphs, the two sprites \(em reach the preview only. An exported PDF has
no disclosure to draw a marker for, and an exported HTML
.RI < details >
is drawn by the reader's own browser. The summary line's band and ink reach all
three.
.TP
.B disclosure_marker_color
Colour. The indicator's ink, both states. Unset, it takes the theme's own
.BR foreground ,
and a theme that states no page of its own keeps the desktop's chevron in the
desktop's colour.
.TP
.B disclosure_glyph
Glyph drawn in place of the collapsed indicator.
.TP
.B disclosure_expanded_glyph
Glyph drawn in place of the expanded indicator.
.TP
.B disclosure_sprite
Sprite drawn in place of the collapsed indicator.
.TP
.B disclosure_expanded_sprite
Sprite drawn in place of the expanded indicator.
.TP
.B disclosure_marker_size
Integer, default 16. The indicator's box. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B disclosure_preview_fg
Colour. The ink of the body-opening fragment shown beside a collapsed summary.
Unset, it keeps the body foreground.
.TP
.B disclosure_band_color
Colour. A band behind the whole summary line, spanning the content column.
Absent unless stated.
.TP
.B disclosure_band_gradient_to_color
Colour. A second stop, making the band a vertical gradient. Ignored where no
fill is stated.
.TP
.B disclosure_band_sprite
Sprite tiled at its natural size across the band. Outranks the fill and the
gradient; a sprite alone is a band.
.TP
.B disclosure_band_radius
Integer, default 0. Clamped 0\-400. Not drawn in an exported PDF.
.TP
.B disclosure_fg
Colour. The ink of the summary line \(em its label, and the body preview beside
it on a collapsed block. Omitted, the summary is ordinary body text. A summary
inside a blockquote takes this ink rather than
.BR blockquote_fg .
.SS Horizontal rule
.TP
.B rule_color
Colour. The
.I ---
rule.
.TP
.B rule_sprite
Sprite tiled horizontally at its natural size across the rule. The rule's height
becomes the tile's own, and
.B rule_thickness
is then ignored.
.TP
.B rule_space
Integer, default 4. Space above and below the rule. Clamped 0\-400.
.TP
.B rule_thickness
Integer, default 1. The flat rule's weight. Read by the preview, the HTML export
and the PDF export alike. Clamped 0\-400.
.SS Selection
.TP
.B selection_bg
Colour. Selection background.
.TP
.B selection_fg
Colour. Ink for selected text. Omitted, it is derived from
.B selection_bg
and the page so that selected text cannot be stranded by accident. State it when
the derived answer is legible but wrong.
.SS Annotations and find
.TP
.B annotation_hl_color
Colour, default
.IR #FFD133_61 .
Annotation highlight overlay.
.TP
.B annotation_chip_bg
Colour. The CriticMarkup comment gutter chip's fill.
.TP
.B annotation_chip_fg
Colour. Ink for the chip's overflow-count numeral.
.TP
.B annotation_chip_sprite
Sprite drawn in place of the flat chip fill. Has no expression in an exported
PDF.
.TP
.B find_hl_all_color
Colour, default
.IR #f6d32d .
Highlight for every find match.
.TP
.B find_hl_current_color
Colour, default
.IR #ff7800 .
Highlight for the current find match.
.SH EXAMPLES
Darken one shipped theme's headings without restating the theme:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
# ~/.config/scribobulate/themes.toml
[themes.sepia]
heading_color = "#3a2a18"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Change an application-wide default for every theme that does not state its own:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[themes.system]
list_step = 36
blockquote_bar_width = 5
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scribobulate/config.toml
Application settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scribobulate/themes.toml
User reading-theme overrides.
.TP
.I /usr/share/scribobulate/themes.toml
The installed reading themes. Useful as a worked reference; edit the user file
rather than this one, which an upgrade replaces.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scribobulate (1)
.PP
The TOML specification:
.UR https://toml.io/
.UE
